                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "promiscuities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67cf4775-e219-370a-be8d-89f2b3204854",
                        "entry_id": "66a98055-2e9c-396e-ad0e-ee34d849ec09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state or quality of being promiscuous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a9a24b2c-56b3-34da-bf0f-be408e055cf5",
                        "entry_id": "66a98055-2e9c-396e-ad0e-ee34d849ec09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Indiscriminateness in the choice of sexual partners."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e829ed0-9478-4614-9509-21217cfba7f8",
                                "sense_id": "a9a24b2c-56b3-34da-bf0f-be408e055cf5",
                                "text": "Experimental variety or what Rey Anthony has called selective promiscuity - is the cornerstone of sane sexual choice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5727726-b4a4-4c0e-b636-2783a0b806a9",
                                "sense_id": "a9a24b2c-56b3-34da-bf0f-be408e055cf5",
                                "text": "I'm not advocating sexual promiscuity but I think it's possible for a woman to have many kinds of sexual relationships with many men and that shouldn't affect the status of the marriage"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e896b010-1df1-4ce6-bc6b-c01c85a9f999",
                                "sense_id": "a9a24b2c-56b3-34da-bf0f-be408e055cf5",
                                "text": "Seeing these happy pairings, I thought of the cheerful promiscuity to come. I felt a growing sexual need, not only for the young women brushing against me in the crowded street..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69d92afa-115e-447c-8150-057de7497594",
                                "sense_id": "a9a24b2c-56b3-34da-bf0f-be408e055cf5",
                                "text": "As she becomes more conscious of her flirtatious power, she is sometimes urged toward promiscuity."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6d714904-57fe-381d-bf1d-3cf3943cc5b4",
                        "entry_id": "66a98055-2e9c-396e-ad0e-ee34d849ec09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "State of being mixed, composed of diverse elements, unsystematic; heterogeneity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "dated",
                            "literary",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2c1bde5-b659-4c5f-92f3-d66012f3012b",
                                "sense_id": "6d714904-57fe-381d-bf1d-3cf3943cc5b4",
                                "text": "While I dressed—for Stroeve wished me to go at once with him to the hospital—he told me that he had arranged for his wife to have a private room, so that she might at least be spared the sordid promiscuity of a ward."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
